  <static seed="1757" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/IntegerAndSquareRoot/MultiplyWithNegativeIntegers30.pg">
    <statement><p>Multiply the following.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ (-2)(-1)(-1)(-1)  }</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ (2)(-2)(-1)(-1) }</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>In multiplication, each pair of negative signs cancel. If all negative signs are canceled, the product is positive; if there is one negative sign left, the product is negative.</p>
<p>a.</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}[t]
   \amp \phantom{{}=}(-2)(-1)(-1)(-1) \\
   \amp = (2)(1)(1)(1) \\
   \amp = {2}
       \end{aligned}</m></p>
<p>b.</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}[t]
   \amp \phantom{{}=}(2)(-2)(-1)(-1) \\
   \amp = -(2)(2)(1)(1) \\
   \amp = {-4}
       \end{aligned}</m></p>
</solution>
